WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.800
So not only were you dealing with the Vietnam protest, but the Civil Rights Movement was going on at the same time.

2
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:14.720
And could you describe any of the involvement of the . . . any other involvement of the National Guard as far as . . .

3
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:15.440
Oh yes, yes.

4
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:19.680
We had two terrific hurricanes when I was there.

5
00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.520
One was Betsy and it flooded all of lower New Orleans.

6
00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:30.630
We had the only amphibious vehicles in the guard: fourteen so-called ducks.

7
00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:35.690
And we and others took 20,000 people off of rooftops in New Orleans, literally.

8
00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:38.770
The homes were flooded, had about eight feet of water,

9
00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:45.450
and brought them up to the military port there at New Orleans, which was a very huge place.

10
00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:52.190
And we put 20,000 people in there and fed and housed them for almost a month.

11
00:00:52.190 --> 00:01:00.850
Of course the other activities, Red Cross and people came in, but it was primarily the military that had to do it all.

12
00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:04.710
We sent troops through all the southern parishes that were flooded.

13
00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:07.970
And they called up most of the guard troops all the way from Shreveport.

14
00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:11.870
And many of them had at least a month's duty.

15
00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:14.370
It was a very trying time.

16
00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:24.850
The storm came in one night and the next afternoon President [Lyndon] Johnson decided to fly down and see the, see the storm.

17
00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:28.110
So I used a duck to . . . Jackson Barracks was flooded,

18
00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:33.670
to get out of Jackson Barracks, and I got on the other side of the Industrial Canal.

19
00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:41.650
I commandeered a police car and raced out to the airport and got there just as the president's plane was taxiing up.

20
00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:47.850
I put him in the front seat of this police car, and I and three Secret Service people jumped in the back end,

21
00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:51.103
crowded in the back, and I brought him down to see the flood.

22
00:01:51.103 --> 00:02:02.770
It was getting on toward night so we got on the industrial bridge there, and here's all these people wading out of chest-high water.

23
00:02:02.770 --> 00:02:06.430
And here stood the president reaching down and helping them out of the water.

24
00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:10.630
So when they'd look up, they were shaking hands with the President of the United States.

25
00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:16.450
And so he greeted them there for a while and basically decided that he was going to go back to Washington.

26
00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:20.850
So I took him back to his plane and flew back to Washington.

27
00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:28.110
I had to prevail upon the Army to send us in mess teams, which they didn't want to do,

28
00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:33.950
because we was trying to feed 20,000 people there and the guard didn't have those kind of facilities.

29
00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:36.790
And then of course we needed all kinds of medical teams.

30
00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:42.090
Inasmuch as we had the only really amphibious vehicles there,

31
00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:50.530
we were just getting hundreds of calls from the police and the hospitals and levee officials and everybody.

32
00:02:50.530 --> 00:02:57.010
It's amazing how many people are injured or how many babies are being born or something when everything's flooded.

33
00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:00.430
So everybody wanted one of these ducks.

34
00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:05.930
And we were making them go as far as they can and trying to keep them running.

35
00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:06.930
Our post was flooded.

36
00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:13.450
Just the very bit up at the front of the levee there, where our headquarters was the only thing that didn't go under water.

37
00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:18.270
So we had our own people to try to take care of down there, as well as all the people in there.

38
00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:21.310
It was quite a trying time.
